Assignment


You are required to fine-tune a 1B LLaMA-based instruction model using both LoRA and QLoRA on Google Colab .. The goal is to understand how parameter-efficient fine-tuning (PEFT) reduces memory usage while maintaining reasonable performance.

First, perform fine-tuning using LoRA, where the base model weights must remain frozen and low-rank adapters should be added only to the attention layers (q_proj, v_proj). Use small hyperparameters such as rank r = 8, 2 epochs, and a learning rate around 2e-4. Record the number of trainable parameters, final training loss, and peak GPU memory usage.

Next, repeat the experiment using QLoRA, where the model must be loaded in 4-bit quantized format (nf4 using bitsandbytes) before applying LoRA adapters. Train under the same settings and again record memory usage and final loss.

After training, generate outputs for 3 test prompts and compare the responses qualitatively.

